==Evolution==
Evolves into '''The Peach Angels''' at level 10

Evolves into '''The Peach Devils''' at level 30 using [[Catfruit]] and XP.

==Strategy/Usage==
Like the other [[Ancient Heroes ULTRA SOULS (Gacha Event)|ULTRA SOULS]], Momotaro has significantly different stats between Normal (spammable) and Evolved Form (high performance), both of which can be used effectively depending on the situation.

==='''Normal Form'''===
Although Momotaro's freeze ability isn't 100% consistent, it comes with a good enough health pool and range, which allows him to be one of the most effective Cats for freezing both Angels and Reds. Depending on the stage, Momotaro could even outperform [[Apple Cat (Super Rare Cat)|iCat]] and [[Juliet Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Juliet the Maiko]].

While it may not be his forte, Momotaro can also be used as a generalist damage dealer, not unlike [[Salon Cat (Rare Cat)|Paris Cat]]. However, Momotaro may need [[Catseye]] boosts to maintain this role.

==='''Evolved Form''' ===
After evolving, The Peach Angels can be a good support unit to rush in and freeze Reds and Angels from a safe enough range. Their quick attack animation and time between attacks make them a good medium-range support unit, while their low cost and recharge time can make for some good stacking and a high probability to freeze enemies.

Their cost-efficiency is The Peach Angels' selling point, as without it, they have no way of justifying their below-average DPS and range. Beware of their speed as well, as they can easily enter the range of enemies that have been knocked back, so mindless use of the [[Cat Cannon]] is not recommended.

==='''True Form'''===
The Peach Devils get enough of a boost to make them worthy as generalists. Their stats are finally in line with their cost, allowing them to rush in, do some damage and not immediately die. Their potential shows in stages where money is scarce and stats are allowed to be a bit lower. They also have decent overall range, meaning they can stick with it pretty well.

Overall, The Peach Devils are a powerful and relatively stackable generalist, with a great ability on top. This makes them a pretty valuable unit and one that can be relied on throughout the whole game. You won't regret investing in them.

==='''Talents'''===
Since The Peach Devils are reliant on stats, '''Attack Buff''' and '''HP Buff''' make them even better, although upgrading them with Catseyes first would be a better investment. Consider these Talents if you already boosted The Peach Devils with Catseyes and have the NP to boost this rusher further. '''Weaken''' makes it so that, if Freeze doesn't activate, the weaken may; it rarely comes into play and doesn't really have a strong effect, but it can be a nice bonus.

'''Freeze Up''' helps and isn't as expensive, but it isn't worth the price to max it out; it's just a single extra second. Buying 2 levels of this Talent will at least give them 100% uptime with [[Fruit Treasures]], so it still helps in some way. '''Resist Slow''' is not a good choice, as while speed is a main factor for the Peach Devils, they're already pretty strong against someone like [[Sunfish Jones]], one of the few common Angel or Red enemies that can slow to begin with. It might be useful for some [[Professor A.]] stages, but the improvement is not worth the NP cost. Furthermore, even when maxed, this Talent merely reduces Slow duration instead of outright negating it.

==='''Ultra Talents'''===
'''Wave Immunity''' is extremely useful in theory, as The Peach Devils can outrange many Wave Attackers and have the stats to function in Wave stages. They notably can counter [[Berserkory]], whose singular Knockback, level 12 Waves and high health makes him difficult to impede. To some extent, this also applies against [[Two Can]] and [[Angelic Beast Rajakong|Rajakong]], as they aren't Immune to Freeze either, although superior anti-Wave options for them also exist.

'''Mini-Wave''' gives them a bit of extra piercing range, allowing them to hit up to 532.5 range away against anything not Immune to Waves. With a 100% chance to occur when fully upgraded, The Peach Devils can potentially snipe an enemy backliner that they usually aren't able to reach and inflict status effects.

'''Knockback''' allows them to, obviously, recover ground by pushing threats away, further hindering their targeted traits if combined with the Weaken and Freeze Talents. As Reds and Angels typically feature aggressive melee pushers, Knockback isn't so detrimental, although it may also cause other units to miss.
