==Trivia==
*Prior to [[Version 2.9.1 Update|Version 2.9.1]], Momotaro had a 50f (1.87-second) attack rate, and The Peach Angels had an 84f (2.8-second) attack rate.
**These faster attack rates are still present in [[The Battle Cats POP!]].
*Prior to [[Version 4.7 Update|Version 4.7]], Momotaro was a part of two other [[Cat Combo]]s: [[Ancient Heroes (Removed Combo)|Ancient Heroes]] and [[Ultra Souls (Removed Combo)|Ultra Souls]].
*This character is based on the Japanese folklore character [[wikipedia:Momotarō|Momotarō]]. The Peach Devils has one of the peaches cut in half with a figure in the middle, alluding to the birth of Momotaro as said in his origin story.
**Momotaro's Japanese description has a small pun: the adjective used to describe him is ''momojiri'' (桃尻), which means "restless" in this context but is spelled with kanji that mean "peach" and "hip".
*The cats accompanying Momotaro as The Peach Angels are dressed as a pheasant, a monkey, and a dog, which are the same animals that the Momotaro of Japanese folklore is said to have befriended on his journey.
**The repetition of the number 4 in his stats, Talents, and Ultra Talents, is most likely a reference to this–counting Momotaro himself, his crew is made up of 4 characters.
*The line, "On a quest to find anyone stronger than him." in Momotaro's description may be a reference to [[Ryu (Uber Rare Cat)|Ryu]], the main protagonist of the ''[[Street Fighter Collaboration Event|Street Fighter]]'' series. His Japanese description even mentions that he trains restlessly.
*The eccentric group seen riding the dune buggy in the Evolved and True Forms is a Japanese-twist reference to post-apocalyptic films such as ''[[wikipedia:Mad Max (film)|Mad Max]]'', ''Doomsday'', or ''Wastelander''.
*The Peach Angels' Japanese name, Bakusō Kyōdai Pīchi Sutā ("Racing Brothers Peach Star") may be a reference to the manga and anime ''[[wikipedia:Bakusō Kyōdai Let's & Go!!|Bakusō Kyōdai Let's & Go!!]]''. In True Form, their dune buggy takes on a color scheme not unlike that of many of Retsu "Let's" Seiba's own Mini 4WD cars, particularly the [[wikia:mini-4wd:Blitzer-Sonic|Blitzer-Sonic]].

